## Context

Migration [[0870]] rebuilt what was already extracted and extracted nothing new.
Measured 2026-09-29 on main (5382a1f5): 392 documents, 369 with a snapshot, 254
with lines (13,089 lines from 253 snapshots), 115 snapshotted documents with
zero lines, 23 with no snapshot (acquisition, out of scope). The information
gain the migration prepares sits in the 115. The join is document, then
`retrievals.sha256`, then `lines.sha256`: `snapshots.csv` has no `document_id`.

The 115 by country: ZAF 49, SEN 28, VNM 25, IDN 13. By type: progress_update 24
(VNM 14, ZAF 9), project_page 27, data_portal 19, official_news 11,
annual_report 7, operator_report 8, project_list 8, implementation_plan 4,
investment_plan 3, approval_document 2, secondary_news 2. All 115 are active;
languages en 59, vi 20, fr 16, empty 20.

Dedup pass done at planning time (documents only, storage contract § 4): no
tier-1 group (same fingerprint) touches the 115; no `edition_of` row exists;
one title matches an already extracted document (to be checked by 1501). Tier 2
(normalised text) was not run: the snapshot bytes are not in a fresh worktree
(DVC), so 1501 runs it where the bytes are.

## Relation to other work

- M1b ([[0833]]) covers only the four M1a documents (2,164 lines) and forbids
  new acquisition, not extraction from archived bytes. It runs first and does
  not wait for these waves; [[1140]] is blocked by 0833, not by extraction.
- Fork B (dedicated document library, Zotero) may change where snapshot bytes
  live. Lines cite `sha256` plus a locator, so the citation survives if the
  byte address is kept. Extraction needs the bytes local; no decision here.
- [[0920]] finishes the 55 pending links of 0874 (missing snapshots, vague
  locators). It overlaps only on the documents it acquires.

## Children, in order

| Wave | Child | Scope |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | [[1501]] | dedup and canonical pass over the 115; fill the 20 empty languages |
| 1 | [[1502]] | 47 periodic or structured documents: progress updates 24, annual and operator reports 15, project lists 8 |
| 1' | [[1505]] | 9 one-off plans and approval documents: implementation plans 4, investment plans 3, approval documents 2 |
| 2 | [[1503]] | 19 data portals, after checking what each snapshot holds |
| 3 | [[1504]] | 40 project pages and news items, as lines under existing identities |

VNM and ZAF first inside each wave: they are the acceptance cases.

## Invariants

- Lines of the 254 extracted documents are byte-identical before and after.
- `make jetp-ledger-check` passes at every child.
- A `line_id` is `<document_id>-<table>-<ordinal>`, appended, never renumbered.
- Duplicates are resolved before extraction, never after.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Children 1501 to 1505 are closed
- [ ] Every one of the 115 documents has lines, or a recorded disposition (duplicate of a canonical document, translation not canonical, or judged without extractable content, with the reason)
- [ ] `docs/jetp-ledger-migration.md` or the observatory How we did this page states the new counts
